v 3
d 'PLUMBER': module to audit changes between two stages of a data pipeline
d
d plumber compares a FROM dataset (an earlier pipeline stage, e.g. raw)
d with a TO dataset (a later stage, e.g. cleaned) at eight selectable
d levels: variable existence, storage type and format, variable labels,
d value-label assignment, value-label definitions, case coverage, cell
d values (eight disjoint numeric change categories, five string
d categories) and value transitions. Results are a long audit table with
d CRITICAL/MAJOR/MINOR/INFO/PASS severities, exportable to .dta and TSV,
d with r() counts and a failon() gate for automated pipelines. Inputs are
d never modified.
d
d KW: data management
d KW: data cleaning
d KW: audit
d KW: reproducibility
d KW: data curation
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Author: Brian W. Mandikiana, SESRI, Qatar University
d Support: email bwmandikiana@gmail.com
d Support: https://github.com/codeatcodecto/plumber/issues
d License: MIT
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261126
d
